3768percentfasterthanepisode9start historical432. Restoredexact554viaindexscript;officialreportbfd5570a349e40cd978aaa3dfcd14585.jsonarchivedunchanged.\n559-561explicitcolumnkernelsbuiltandscreened:transpose-only555hasoriginalstrides,soitisaunary-expressioncontrol,nottheclaimedphysicalcolmajorcontrol. Actualdiagnosticstridesoriginal(400,1),transpose-expression(400,1),preallocatedcolumn(1,512). Preserveoriginalhypothesisandcorrectinterpretationhere.\n562-564exactlowrankcostenergycontractionsbuilt:Kkernelunchanged,weightedfeatures/norms/observedlabelindicatorsform22-columnresponse; controlsusesplit12+10columnsorpreweightedlabelcost10fields. MoreflopsbutavoidsdenseK*Cpass. Allscreenpending,notretained.\n\n559-561explicitcolumnKall30pass,means0.0475-0.0500,notcompelling.562-564exactcostenergyfactoringall30pass,worstnRMSE0.00702565-0.00702570;fields22mean0.042396,split12+10mean0.049298,preweightedlabelsmean0.043624. Freshround5comparesbest554against559/561/562/564;pickformalcandidateonlyifimprovementisplausible.\nReportedseedmeansfor554:1010.038438,2020.036844,3030.038237,4040.037600,5050.036886. Itwasfasterthan547in20/30casesandsavedmean0.000993761s,andfasterthanhistorical432in22/30cases,savingmean0.001827993s. Thisisdescriptiveofficialreportcomparison,notaclaimofadditionalformalstatisticalsignificance.\nAll18syntheticpublicreorderspassedfor432/547/512/554/555;worst0.00851313,minrho0.99995404,mintop0.994667. Targetscomputedfreshusingcanonical000;all90qualityrecordsandshuffleseedsarchived.\n\nFreshround5medians5540.0426315,5590.0496287,5610.0530554,5620.0423650,5640.0415857. ExplicitcolumnKloses; lowrankexactcostenergyfieldsremainpromising. 564passes18syntheticreordercasesworst0.0085131123/minrho0.9999540462/mintop0.994667. Selected564forfifthandfinalcompleteofficialevaluation. Best554preserved;nootherownnumericworkconcurrent.\n\n564 complete official final result: statusok, raw0.061441357034103326, score0.8821821845358105, all30/all270qualityvalid, exacthashcec185be3b526a4ac4beb2d90522f8f89d08d13022ae21f1ccdac22f06d9ee73. Slower than measuredbest554; reject and restoreexact554 via index. Originalreport347af298fa0344ffb4b451cbe0a26e03.json archived unchanged. Noofficialpending.\nFinal diagnostic profile excludes inputreads, elapsed0.128227, pointdual0.058/class0.021/coupling0.020; timing differs substantially from formalreport and is not a score. All67 candidate screens contain30 cases;2010 totalpubliccasequality records. 68source snapshots;62 locallyvalid,5numericalfailures,5completeofficialevaluations. Eighteenpublicpermutationcases across6sources yield108canonical-comparisonrecords. Finalselectedhasha73d8c270d13c6defb541b70facabbcf7f909dd3911b6a774e200d531691823d.\n\nFinal verification initial assertion counted protected infrastructure directory entries; corrected to ordinary submission files only. Error preserved in episode9_verification_initial_error.txt. Exact source and frozen launcher verified; only method.py/solve.sh ordinary files, protected directories untouched. No evaluation pending.\n# Episode 11 mechanisms\n\nAll mechanisms derive geometry from the supplied arrays and preserve every first-batch empirical class support and every point batch. Local quality diagnostics use own canonical public-array computations saved by earlier episodes. They never access protected targets.\n\n## Persistent hard class reduced costs\nAt the first globally hard class stage define `R = C - f[:,None] - g[None,:]`. A parallel hard update has residual increments `df = rowmin(R) - eps*log(1/m)` and `dg = colmin(R) - eps*log(1/n)`. Thus `f_new=f+.5*df`, `g_new=g+.5*dg`, and `R_new=R-.5*df[:,None]-.5*dg[None,:]`. Keeping R across the contiguous hard suffix eliminates full dense residual allocations and subtraction of large absolute duals at every stage. Active/mask controls are preserved. The final reference extrapolation is `g += .25*dg`, so the last residual shift can combine `.5` and `.25` into `.75*dg`. Final objective is unchanged: mean(f+rowmin(R)-.1*lb)+mean(g+colmin(R)-.1*la). Variations include ordinary in-place updates, fused rank-two BMM, and scalar-only mean-dual tracking.\n\n## Rank-two residual construction\n`f[:,None]+g[None,:] = [f,ones]  @  [ones,g]`. Torch addmm/baddbmm applies the additive residual in one native call. Column-major class storage uses the transposed product `[g,ones]  @  [ones,f]`. This saves dense passes in principle but multiplication dispatch can cost more than broadcasting. Keep controls with separate output allocation and in-place output aliasing.\n\n## One-sided padded class geometry\nSort actual reference supports by observed labels and retain only candidate-side padding. Potentials f have `(candidate_label,candidate_point,reference_label)` shape, g have `(candidate_label,actual_reference_point)` shape. Segmented row transforms operate on contiguous reference label segments. Native column reductions operate over candidate points, eliminating one of the two segmented reductions used in episode 9. This layout removes reference padding but still needs dense expansion of reference-label-specific candidate potentials.\n\n## Direct dual increments\nWhenever transformed dual `ft=f+shift-eps*(log(rowmass)+lb)` is immediately followed by `df=ft-f`, compute df directly. For point kernels the analogous update is `f += -.5*eps*(log(rowmass)+lb)`, and similarly g. Fallbacks retain stable direct transforms. Only floating reduction/addition order changes.\n\n## Fused final point powers/reduction\nIn the reference-only final stage, K after row balancing is raised to q=4, then summed by column. The final K is never used again. `sum(K**4) = norm_4(K)**4 = norm_2(K**2)**2`. Native vector norms may fuse a power and reduction, avoiding dense write/read passes. The root can cancel directly in logs: `log(sum(K**4))=4*log(norm_4(K))=2*log(norm_2(K**2))`. Sum positivity retains the stable logsumexp fallback. A square-root kernel storage control adapts dual balancing factors to fourth roots and obtains all marginals via norm2 squared.\n\n## Direct centered class residual geometry\nInitial class duals are f0_i=||a_i||²/2 + E||b||²/2 - a_i dot E(b), and similarly g0_j. Therefore R0=C-f0-g0 = -(a_i-Ea) dot (b_j-Eb) + Ea dot Eb - E||a||²/2 - E||b||²/2. The scalar offset is negative mean(C). Solve using R0 and zero initial duals, then restore mean(f0)+mean(g0)=2mean(C) to the pair objective. Computing the centered product skips original dense unary costs and first-stage subtraction. Original-temperature geometry and masks remain. A control forms the gauge via original geometry before subtraction; another centers the twenty unique supports once before packing and derives offsets from their unique means/norms. The first unshifted exponential is allowed only if the actual maximum residual exponent is below60, with original stable shifted fallback otherwise.\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
