lures. `episode7_build_round1.py`, `episode7_build_round2.py`, `episode7_official.py`, `episode7_screen_missing.py` and `finalize_episode7.py` preserve core drivers.\n/tmp/research_history/episode_7_continuing_notes.md:45:- Earlier `screen_all.py` treats its first argument as baseline and skips reporting it. Rounds3-10 initially omitted their first candidate from logs. Missing direct screens were completed by `episode7_screen_missing.py`, which compares every listed source to prior locally computed canonical public-array outputs and never changes those caches. Preserve original incomplete logs; index combines them with follow-up results.415NaN failure is now explicitly recorded for all30. No missing official cases.\n/tmp/research_history/episode_7_continuing_notes.md:47:- Fresh-process comparison432median0.0523977 versus4340.0510058 was diagnostic only; fullprotocol rejected434. Original observed timing lists are saved in `bench_episode7_round1_fresh.log`.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
