{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_82", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat >> /tmp/research_history/episode12_derivations.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Fused intermediate recurrence\n\nThe traced public303Gaussian016 case performs five ordinary dyadic kernel recurrences per point pair, with positive marginals throughout, then a hard final reference transform. Thus final-only power fusion cannot address its repeated hot loop. For q=4, Knew=K**4*(m/rs)**2[:,None]*(n/cs)**2[None,:]. A native four-operand einsum can instead form B=K**2*(m/rs)[:,None]*(n/cs)[None,:] in one pass, then Knew=B**2 in one more. A six-operand version computes Knew in one contraction. Controls fuse only the original two sqrt balancing factors; write to an aliasing output vs a separate allocated result; or apply the same class recurrence with padded inactive factors. Finite-marginal direct fallbacks are preserved. These change actual intermediate recurrences, unlike the final-only contractions.\n\n## Disposable terminal hard costs\n\nAt a terminal hard reference update, gnew=.5*(g+colmin(C-f)-eps*la). C is disposable because coupling was already computed. Mutating C-=f avoids a dense temporary. The final candidate c-transform becomes f+rowmin(C-gnew)-.1*lb. Both Torch and zero-copy NumPy controls restore that exact unary f contribution before existing point calibration. Full cost construction copies each original point-pair slice, so in-place mutation never corrupts other batches.\n\n## NumPy complete hard cache blocks\n\nEarlier NumPy controls traversed the complete class matrix at every hard stage. Here loop interchange and entry-shift localization permit a complete10/25/50-pair block to remain in cache across every hard refinement, final g extrapolation and both final transforms. NumPy minima and in-place broadcasts operate on shared Torch-backed float32 residual/potential views; all masks, temperatures and class objective divisors stay identical. This isolates NumPy dispatch in a cache-resident suffix instead of repeating the old entire-matrix sweep.\nEOF\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
