nary submission files exactly method.py and solve.sh; method size{len(source)}bytes.\n\nRetention uses the fastest complete official quality-valid aggregate, including historical best. Initial689 repeats previous selected671 bytes; its improved raw is timing variation, not a new algorithmic gain. No own numerical workload overlapped any complete official evaluation.\n\n## Complete official measurements\n\n| Source | Raw seconds | Score | Exact evaluator source hash |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n{rows}\n\nOriginal evaluator stdout and reports are archived unchanged in each source directory; source bytes match every reported hash. No source with only local diagnostics is retained.\n\n## New mechanisms and decisions\n\n-690–694/699–704 implicit separable kernel factors: keep one or both row/column normalizers outside dense exponential kernels, weighted GEMM/BMM marginals, scalar-normalized powers and direct fallback. Logarithmic and purely algebraic controls all30pass. Point variants lose fresh timings; class row693 looked promising but official loses.\n-695–698 share first class/point empirical feature geometry: full unpadded GEMM or homogeneous12-dimensional product plus padded class gathers, or reconstruct original point geometry from packed class BMM. All30pass; fresh gains inconclusive. Gather overhead offsets product reuse.\n-705–708 full augmented point costs and grouped coupling: independent-pair full-cost705 and6-response global/block2-response coupling contractions preserve each pair'\"'s temperature/marginals/expectation. All30pass. Grouping slower; official705 loses to initial689.\n-709–714/721–725 entire hard class suffix cache blocks: loop interchange keeps10/20/25/50/100 pairs resident across every hard refinement and final transforms. Entry shifts can also be localized. Row-major late-copy724 is slower. Exact standalone block25 candidate722 and full-cost combination725 were most promising. See complete official rows for retention.\n-715–720/726 fused final point fourth powers and coupling energy: native NumPy four/five-operand contractions, weight-first and float64 range controls. All30pass; no robust speed win. Diagnostic303Gaussian016 has no point fallback and finaleps<=2 in all6pairs, so these final-fourth changes do not address its repeated loop.\n-727–734 fused intermediate recurrences: native einsum combines balancing and squared/fourth powers in real recurring stages. All30pass but markedly slower (point multioperand mean~.159s, combined~.181s). In-place versus separate allocation does not help.\n-735–737 disposable terminal hard point costs: subtract final candidate dual in place, restore its unary vector after final candidate minimum. Clone-first residual is an allocation control. All30pass with rounding-level changes; measured outcomes determine retention.\n-738–742 native NumPy complete hard cache blocks and terminal point minima. These differ from older NumPy sweeps by completing every hard stage inside each resident block. All30pass; fresh timing regime noisy, no established improvement over retained source.\n\nAll methods preserve every empirical first-batch support, original contiguous1024point batches, selected finite annealing and array-derived transport. There are no learned weights, output tables, input caches or solver I/O. Equations and implementation tradeoffs are in episode12_derivations.md.\n\n## Validation and continuation\n\n-{len(index)}source snapshots; {audit['local_screens']}complete all30local screens; {audit['local_valid']}locally valid; {audit['local_case_records']}local quality records; {len(official)}complete official evaluations.\n-Three fresh-process rounds contain{audit['fresh_process_calls']}independent calls over3publiccases in alternating order. Large timing variation is preserved in rawlists; local timings are never reported as official scores.\n-Nine new public-array resampling/size diagnostics (N2200/M1800, N3600/M2400, N1800/M1200), with freshly recomputed canonical000targets. Seven defined targets: all4candidates pass, worstnRMSE~.0067112, minimumrho~.99995669, minimumtop .99. Two canonical outer couplings did not converge, so their targets are explicitly undefined; no numerical comparison is claimed for them. Original failing driver/stdout, exact error notes and corrected complete attempt records are retained. Stress is diagnostic, outside the fixed official30case protocol.\n-The first index draft assumed wrong report field names; it was corrected before execution, with original unexecuted draft preserved. No evaluator report was altered.\n\n\"'`episode_12_index.json`, `episode12_official_summary.json`, `episode_12_final_selection.json` and `episode12_final_audit.json` preserve selection and exact evidence. `python /tmp/research_history/episode12_index.py --restore` reproduces restoration. Builders1–10, manifests/screens, fresh timings, trace, stress records, slower sources and working notes are under `/tmp/research_history`. Previous notes are preserved as episode12_prior_notes.md and episode_11_continuing_notes.md.\n\nNext episode should start from selected exact bytes. Complete hard-suffix cache blocks and disposable terminal cost arithmetic are useful building blocks, but confirm combinations through full official evaluation. Native multioperand einsum recurrence fusion is slow. Grouped coupling and implicit point factors do not win. Read earlier summaries before repeating generic groups, sparse graphs, coresets, reduced precision, polynomial coupling or aggressive truncation, which already have extensive failures/slower controls.\n\nNo protected assets, evaluator code/targets, private inputs, credentials, environment variables, hidden tests, other trajectories, network, installations or subagents were accessed. Only method.py changed as a submission asset; solve.sh remains frozen. Research artifacts are outside the submission directory.\n'\"'''\nPath('/tmp/research_notes.md').write_text(notes);(root/'episode_12_continuing_notes.md').write_text(notes)\nprint(json.dumps(audit,indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
